[size=2]Also see: [b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/articles/12531]Mod Author: Feed Notifications[/url][/b] ([font=Courier New]Notify[/font], divert, API toast icons).[/size]

This article is for list authors who want to assign specific icons to Feed toasts, or determined players who want to get their setup [i]just so[/i].
[size=3]
Each Feed section can resolve a per-message icon from hand-edited text files under [font=Courier New]SKSE/Plugins/COG/gizmos/feed/[/font]. Players customize them without Papyrus; authors can ship overrides in a mod the same way. This page covers the grammar and the per-section extras.[/size]

If a mod passes its own icon with a notification, disk rules lose — that path is covered in [b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/articles/12531]Mod Author: Feed Notifications[/url][/b]. Icon file locations still follow [b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/articles/12506]Intermediate: Fonts and Icons[/url][/b] (authors registering imports: [b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/articles/12532]Mod Author: Fonts and Icons[/url][/b]).

[center][img width=250]https://i.ibb.co/qL0ZKvB1/Dragonborn-Knotwork-Left.png[/img] [size=6]Where the Files Live[/size] [img width=250]https://i.ibb.co/gL2J92Hx/Dragonborn-Knotwork-Right.png[/img][/center]

[color=#bf9000][size=5]Folders[/size][/color]

Under your mod (Data-rooted archive) or under COG after install:

[code]SKSE/Plugins/COG/gizmos/feed/
notifications/
inventory/
location/
effects/
skills/[/code]

Each folder has a shipped [b][font=Courier New]_COG.txt[/font][/b] (installed with the mod) plus any override [font=Courier New]*.txt[/font] you add. While you can technically edit [b][font=Courier New]_COG.txt[/font][/b], any update or reinstall will wipe it, so you're better off adding a new file with your own rules in your Overwrite directory or game directory.
[b]
Last wins:[/b] so for filenames, Z will beat A, and inside files, rules at the bottom will beat those at the top; the same left-hand match in a later file or later line replaces the earlier one. [font=Courier New]_COG.txt[/font] sorts first, so it has the lowest precedence: your [font=Courier New]MyPack.txt[/font] wins over it.

Comment lines start with [font=Courier New]#[/font]. Empty lines are ignored.

[center][img width=250]https://i.ibb.co/qL0ZKvB1/Dragonborn-Knotwork-Left.png[/img] [size=6]Shared Grammar[/size] [img width=250]https://i.ibb.co/gL2J92Hx/Dragonborn-Knotwork-Right.png[/img][/center]

[color=#bf9000][size=5]Shape of a Rule[/size][/color]

[code]# comment
name equals `Chef's Hat` = Clothing/hat-chef.svg
name contains `wine` = Food and Drink/bottle.svg
form equals `Skyrim.esm:0001397D` = Weapons/broadsword.svg[/code]

[list]
[*][b]Kinds (all sections):[/b] [font=Courier New]name[/font], [font=Courier New]form[/font][/*]
[*][b]Operations:[/b] [font=Courier New]equals[/font], [font=Courier New]notequals[/font], [font=Courier New]contains[/font], [font=Courier New]notcontains[/font][/*]
[*][b]Match text[/b] sits in backticks; matching is case-insensitive; spaces inside backticks matter[/*]
[*]Multiple operators on one line are [b]AND[/b]ed (same kind)[/*]
[*]Icon path is relative to [font=Courier New]PrismaUI/views/COG/assets/icons/[/font] (import paths work once COG can resolve them like other icons)[/*]
[/list]

Incomplete lines like [font=Courier New]name Foo = path[/font] (no operator / backticks) are [b]invalid[/b]. Use the operator form with backticks around the match text. Unknown kinds for a section are skipped with a log warning (for example an [font=Courier New]av[/font] rule under [font=Courier New]inventory/[/font] does nothing there).

[center][img width=250]https://i.ibb.co/qL0ZKvB1/Dragonborn-Knotwork-Left.png[/img] [size=6]Per Section[/size] [img width=250]https://i.ibb.co/gL2J92Hx/Dragonborn-Knotwork-Right.png[/img][/center]

[color=#bf9000][size=5]Notifications[/size][/color]

[font=Courier New]gizmos/feed/notifications/[/font]

[list]
[*]Extra kinds: none (base only)[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]name[/font] = translated toast text (what you see in the Feed)[/*]
[*]Resolve order (if [color=#b45f06]Show icons[/color] is on): Icon from the mod's notify call → matching rule → Feed Notification Defaults icon
[/*]
[/list]

[code]name equals `Bloodlust Extended` = Werewolf/wolf.svg
name contains `werewolf` = Werewolf/wolf.svg[/code]

[color=#bf9000][size=5]Inventory[/size][/color]

[font=Courier New]gizmos/feed/inventory/[/font]

Extra kinds (from the item):

[list]
[*][b]Kind:[/b] [font=Courier New]keyword[/font]. [b]Examples:[/b] [font=Courier New]WeapTypeSword[/font][/*]
[*][b]Kind:[/b] [font=Courier New]formtype[/font]. [b]Examples:[/b] [font=Courier New]weap[/font], [font=Courier New]armo[/font], [font=Courier New]alch[/font], ...[/*]
[*][b]Kind:[/b] [font=Courier New]weapontype[/font]. [b]Examples:[/b] [font=Courier New]onehandsword[/font], [font=Courier New]bow[/font], ...[/*]
[*][b]Kind:[/b] [font=Courier New]armortype[/font]. [b]Examples:[/b] [font=Courier New]lightarmor[/font], [font=Courier New]heavyarmor[/font], [font=Courier New]clothing[/font][/*]
[*][b]Kind:[/b] [font=Courier New]armorslot[/font]. [b]Examples:[/b] [font=Courier New]head[/font], [font=Courier New]body[/font], [font=Courier New]hands[/font], [font=Courier New]shield[/font], ...[/*]
[/list]

Fallback if nothing matches: Feed Default Icon → [font=Courier New]Treasure/bag.svg[/font].

[code]formtype equals `alch` = Alchemy/potion.svg
keyword equals `WeapTypeBow` = Weapons/bow.svg
weapontype equals `onehandsword` = Weapons/broadsword.svg
armortype equals `heavyarmor` = Armour/breastplate-male.svg
armorslot equals `shield` = Weapons/shield-simple.svg
name contains `wine` = Food and Drink/bottle.svg
form equals `Skyrim.esm:0001397D` = Weapons/broadsword.svg[/code]

[color=#bf9000][size=5]Location[/size][/color]

[font=Courier New]gizmos/feed/location/[/font]

[list]
[*]Extra kind: [font=Courier New]kind[/font] with match text [font=Courier New]discovery[/font] or [font=Courier New]current[/font][/*]
[*][font=Courier New]name[/font] = translated place text[/*]
[/list]

[code]name contains `Whiterun` = Camping/map.svg
kind equals `current` = Camping/compass.svg
kind equals `discovery` = Camping/map.svg[/code]

Empty resolve → UI keeps the Feed's discovery / current default icons.

[color=#bf9000][size=5]Active Effects[/size][/color]

[font=Courier New]gizmos/feed/effects/[/font]

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]form[/font] matches the [b]magic effect[/b] (MGEF), not the spell[/*]
[*]Extras: [font=Courier New]keyword[/font], [font=Courier New]formtype[/font], [font=Courier New]av[/font] (actor value / school candidates), [font=Courier New]archetype[/font] (effect archetype string)[/*]
[*]Fallback: Feed [font=Courier New]effectIcon[/font] → [font=Courier New]Magic/sparkles.svg[/font][/*]
[/list]

[code]av equals `Health` = Alchemy/potion.svg
av equals `Destruction` = Survival/fire.svg
av contains `Resist` = Weapons/shield-reinforced.svg
archetype equals `Invisibility` = Magic/sparkles.svg
archetype equals `SlowTime` = Actions/wait.svg
archetype equals `Werewolf` = Werewolf/wolf.svg[/code]

[color=#bf9000][size=5]Skills[/size][/color]

[font=Courier New]gizmos/feed/skills/[/font]

[list]
[*]Base kinds only[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]name[/font] candidates include HUD banner text, ActorValue string (e.g. [font=Courier New]OneHanded[/font]), and localized AV name[/*]
[*]Level-up / Level Progress can use the Feed's [font=Courier New]levelIcon[/font]; skill toasts use [font=Courier New]skillIcon[/font] when rules miss[/*]
[/list]

[code]name equals `OneHanded` = Weapons/broadsword.svg
name equals `One-Handed` = Weapons/broadsword.svg
name contains `Archery` = Weapons/bow.svg
name contains `Smithing` = Crafting/anvil.svg
name contains `Sneak` = Clothing/hood.svg[/code]

[center][img width=250]https://i.ibb.co/qL0ZKvB1/Dragonborn-Knotwork-Left.png[/img] [size=6]Shipping Overrides[/size] [img width=250]https://i.ibb.co/gL2J92Hx/Dragonborn-Knotwork-Right.png[/img][/center]

[color=#bf9000][size=5]As a List or Mod Author[/size][/color]

Ship your own file, not a replacement [font=Courier New]_COG.txt[/font] (deploy may refresh [font=Courier New]_COG.txt[/font] on COG updates):

[code]SKSE/Plugins/COG/gizmos/feed/notifications/
MyModNotifications.txt[/code]

Name it so it sorts after [font=Courier New]_COG.txt[/font] if you intend to override (almost anything does). Players can add personal overrides the same way in Overwrite or a small patch mod.

[color=#bf9000][size=5]Common Pitfalls[/size][/color]

[list]
[*]Editing [font=Courier New]_COG.txt[/font] in the main COG mod: next update can wipe it; use a sibling [font=Courier New]*.txt[/font].[/*]
[*]Forgetting backticks around match text.[/*]
[*]Expecting a notification rule to beat an icon the mod attached to the toast: that icon always wins.[/*]
[*]Putting rules in the wrong section folder.[/*]
[/list]
